I just played to test it out, and honestly, even tho it's your regular "Indie" RPG, it has some fun elements;
- You choose a class(Thief, Warrior and Mage) and then you choose a school that focuses on several things, so for exemple, you chose a Thief, that specializes in Agility, crits etc, but then you choose the school that focuses on healing and buffs. So there is a lot of mix-ups you can do here.
- The plot seems, for what I played, a normal plot, everything is fine and♥♥♥♥♥♥goes down and you need to do all the work;
- There are some "bugs" audio wise, some sounds don't seem as clear. In particular, the part where you enter the car to go the Missile Launch site, the music keeps playing while other audio goes on the background, and that takes the mood off.
A decent game if you don't have much to do.

